{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"peppery-dire-indianabat","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context\n\n`docs/architecture.md` describes RP-05 as pending. The module docstring in `src/rebar/_cli/_registry.py` still calls the registry shadow scaffolding. The closed grapy-cynical-copepod epic and pettish-snippy-rasbora record the completed registry cutover. ADR 0100 remains the historical decision record.\n\n## Plan\n\n- Describe `ROUTES`, lazy handler and parser references, runtime registry dispatch, generated help inputs, and `CAPABILITIES` as the implemented boundary.\n- Remove migration-pending wording from current architecture documentation.\n- Correct the stale registry module docstring without changing executable behavior.\n- Preserve ADR 0100 and generated-source ownership.\n- Run focused registry, help coverage, help generation, and import-isolation checks.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Architecture documentation identifies RP-05 as implemented.\n- [ ] Architecture documentation describes every listed registry boundary component.\n- [ ] The registry module docstring describes the implemented authority without shadow-scaffolding language.\n- [ ] ADR 0100 and registry behavior remain unchanged.\n- [ ] Generated help inputs remain registry-owned.\n- [ ] Focused registry, help, generation, and import-isolation checks pass.","id":"f1f3-4a26-d67b-4cbe","parent_id":"b8bf-a5aa-2f4d-44d4","priority":1,"tags":["documentation","accuracy","f30b"],"ticket_type":"task","title":"F30B document the implemented RP-05 boundary"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787512094472372001,"uuid":"b3cca4ac-e653-4394-9e33-706b6a0b79ea"}